# Comms / gateway / database (draft)

Full text: [docs/context/03-comms-gateway-database.md](docs/context/03-comms-gateway-database.md). Frozen on-wire today: AMP (DOC-005).

Candidate rules (unresolved vs AMP/baseline):

- Treat the radio payload as untrusted. Validate frame, length, CRC, version, schema, node ID, then de-dup and sequence analysis. Never ingest corrupt packets into measurement tables.
- `protocol_version` ≠ `firmware_version`. Never decode v2 with v1 rules.
- At-least-once on air + gateway de-duplication. Missing ≠ zero. Keep `timestamp` and `received_at` separate.
- Persist `sampling_decisions` (why sampling changed), radio RSSI/SNR, quality flags.
- Dashboard must not query SQLite. FastAPI + WebSocket. AI must not know SQL table names.
- Offline-first: internet down must not stop LoRa, DB, local AI, LAN dashboard.
- MQTT, Prometheus, and Docker are optional in this candidate constitution — do not add them by default.

Do not rewrite AMP, ICD-001/002, or the TimescaleDB baseline until the conflict matrix is decided.
